Subject: Post-AGI Alpha Hunt =E2=80=94 Certification Bandwidth & Physical-A=
I
Permission Scarcity
To: tradesprior@gmail.com

Post-AGI Alpha Hunt =E2=80=94 10 Sep 2026

Highest-signal fresh rabbit hole: CERTIFICATION BANDWIDTH / SAFETY-CASE
THROUGHPUT

Core thesis
AI can improve much faster than the institutions allowed to certify
physical deployment. That turns certification itself into a scarce
resource. The deployment bottleneck is no longer only whether a robot,
autonomous lab, data center or AI-controlled machine works; it is whether
its safety case can be independently inspected, documented, tested and
approved fast enough.

Why this matters now
=E2=80=A2 NVIDIA launched Halos for Robotics in June 2026 and created the f=
irst
ANAB-accredited inspection program for physical-AI safety, explicitly
designed to prepare systems for third-party certification under standards
including IEC 61508, ISO 13849 and ISO/IEC TR 5469.
=E2=80=A2 T=C3=9CV Rheinland is already evaluating NVIDIA IGX Thor, Halos O=
S and
Holoscan Sensor Bridge for functional-safety certification readiness.
=E2=80=A2 A real commercial AMR example from Quasi Robotics required six mo=
nths of
comprehensive conformity assessment before CE/UKCA certification.
=E2=80=A2 SGS says its Digital Trust business grew 38% in H1 2026; AI assur=
ance and
cybersecurity were explicit drivers. SGS=E2=80=99s broader group organic gr=
owth was
only 5.6%, showing how much faster this trust layer is already growing.
=E2=80=A2 Bureau Veritas launched a direct AI-systems audit product in Apri=
l 2026,
combining on-site audit, document review and direct testing for EU AI Act
readiness.

New kernel primitive
PermissionBandwidth =3D certified deployments / unit time

And a derived ratio:
CertificationDebt =3D (rate of system/model change =C3=97 safety-critical s=
urface
area =C3=97 validation depth) / certification capacity

If AI model or control-stack iteration occurs monthly while certification
takes quarters, CertificationDebt compounds. The economically valuable
companies may be those with accredited labs, recognized assessors, test
infrastructure, proprietary safety datasets, and enough trained humans to
sign off systems.

Public exposures

   1. SGS (SGSN / SGSOY) =E2=80=94 highest direct signal. H1 2026 Digital T=
rust
   growth 38%; certification and AI assurance already contributing. Current
   forward P/E is roughly 21=E2=80=9323x depending venue/data source. Not c=
heap, but
   not an AI-style multiple either.
   2. Bureau Veritas (BVI) =E2=80=94 less pure, but current forward P/E aro=
und
   16.5=E2=80=9318x. It has a live AI Act assessment offering and a global
   certification footprint. This may be the better valuation setup if
   AI/physical-AI assurance becomes structurally important.
   3. Intertek (ITRK) =E2=80=94 similar structural exposure, but current va=
luation
   around 20x forward earnings and corporate-event noise from recent EQT
   takeover interest makes it a less clean thesis vehicle.

Falsifiers
=E2=80=A2 Regulators accept self-certification or software-only evidence fo=
r most
physical-AI systems.
=E2=80=A2 NVIDIA/large OEMs internalize most testing and certification econ=
omics.
=E2=80=A2 Safety standards stabilize enough that incremental validation per
software/model update becomes trivial.
=E2=80=A2 Certification staffing scales linearly with demand and pricing po=
wer
fails to appear.

SECOND RABBIT HOLE: POSITION-FEEDBACK BANDWIDTH

Physical AI cannot act directly from intelligence; it needs increasingly
precise feedback about where things actually are. Encoders, probes and
metrology form the feedback channel between AI-generated intent and
physical motion.

Renishaw is a useful proof point. Its Position Measurement revenue grew
21.6% at constant FX over the first nine months of FY2026, while
semiconductor/electronics demand drove a substantial order-book expansion.
The company then reported record Q4 revenue, +27% YoY, and roughly +14%
FY2026 revenue growth. The stock has already rerated strongly and trades
around 25=E2=80=9326x forward earnings, so this is more useful as evidence =
for the
primitive than as an obvious cheap trade.

New primitive:
PhysicalFeedbackIntensity =3D value of position/measurement feedback per un=
it
of physical automation

The interesting downstream screen is not simply robotics vendors. It is
suppliers where more autonomous axes, tighter tolerances, and faster motion
all increase feedback-content per machine.

THIRD RABBIT HOLE: SAFETY-FENCE HARDWARE / AGENT-TO-INSTRUMENT PERMISSIONIN=
G

Recent autonomous-lab work is converging on explicit physical-world safety
primitives. LAP proposes cryptographically bound operator-confirmation
tokens, first-class instrument reservations, sample locking,
calibration-anchored measurements and safety handshakes. A separate 2026
trapped-ion system places a hardware safety gate between LLM-written
control code and the experiment because unchecked code can damage expensive
apparatus.

This suggests a new layer between MCP-style software tools and physical
devices:
agent -> signed permission -> safety controller -> instrument

That layer could favor functional-safety PLCs, certified servo drives,
interlock systems, safety MCUs and specialist inspection/certification
vendors. NVIDIA=E2=80=99s Halos ecosystem already names Infineon, NXP,
STMicroelectronics and Texas Instruments as safety-silicon contributors.

Kernel additions from this run
=E2=80=A2 permission_bandwidth
=E2=80=A2 certification_debt
=E2=80=A2 safety_case_latency
=E2=80=A2 accredited_lab_capacity
=E2=80=A2 physical_feedback_intensity
=E2=80=A2 safety_fence_density
=E2=80=A2 model_update_to_recertification_ratio

Ranking by expected alpha

   1. Certification bandwidth / safety-case throughput =E2=80=94 9.4/10
   2. Physical-AI assurance companies, especially SGS/Bureau Veritas =E2=80=
=94
   8.9/10
   3. Agent-to-instrument safety fences =E2=80=94 8.7/10
   4. Position-feedback intensity =E2=80=94 8.4/10

The important conceptual update is that permission scarcity should be
modeled as a throughput constraint, not just a regulatory risk. In a world
where cognition/software changes almost instantly, organizations that can
legally and credibly convert novel intelligence into deployable physical
action may become toll roads.

